<% @title = "Amber brand system — Amber Framework" %>
<% @meta = "The Amber Framework V2 logo, color, typography, and visual-language reference." %>

<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="site-container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Brand system · V2</p>
    <h1>Technical clarity,<br>warmly expressed.</h1>
    <p>The Amber V2 visual language pairs faceted crystal geometry with an editorial voice: precise enough for the terminal, welcoming enough for a first framework.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container brand-grid">
      <article class="brand-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Mark</p>
        <h2>The Amber crystal</h2>
        <p>Use the faceted mark as the primary Amber Framework identifier. Preserve its proportions, surrounding space, and warm orange palette.</p>
        <img src="/assets/brand/amber-crystal.svg" width="220" height="220" alt="Amber Framework faceted crystal logo" style="margin: 36px auto 8px; width: 180px;">
      </article>
      <article class="brand-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Typography</p>
        <h2 style="font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);">Crystal clear.</h2>
        <p>Fraunces carries the expressive, human layer. Manrope handles navigation and body copy. A system monospace keeps commands visually exact.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="brand-card" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;">
        <p class="eyebrow">Color system</p>
        <h2>Warm core, distinct ecosystem.</h2>
        <div class="swatches">
          <div class="swatch" style="background:#fffaf3;">Canvas<br>#FFFAF3</div>
          <div class="swatch" style="background:#f47716; color:white;">Amber<br>#F47716</div>
          <div class="swatch" style="background:#147f80; color:white;">Grant teal<br>#147F80</div>
          <div class="swatch" style="background:#8051a7; color:white;">Gemma violet<br>#8051A7</div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
